# %%APP_NAME%%

A [Forge](https://github.com/rocketinsidecorp/forge-rust) application organized
around hexagonal architecture boundaries:

```text
src/domain          business rules; no I/O, HTTP, database or vendor types
src/application     commands, queries, use cases and ports
src/adapters        HTTP and other protocol translation
src/infrastructure  concrete database, cache, queue and telemetry mechanisms
src/bootstrap       composition root and process lifecycle
```

`tests/architecture.rs` fails when an inner ring imports an outer one.
%%if views%%

## Views

Pages are rendered on the server, as in Rails
([ADR 0022](https://github.com/rocketinsidecorp/forge-rust/blob/main/docs/adr/0022-server-rendered-views.md)):

```text
templates/layouts/application.html  layout: CSRF meta tag, stylesheet, import map
templates/layouts/_flash.html       one-shot notice/alert messages
templates/welcome/index.html        the page served at /
src/adapters/http/views/            view models checked against the templates at compile time
assets/                             CSS, JavaScript and the logo, digested and embedded by build.rs
```

Templates use [Askama](https://askama.rs): `{{ value }}` is HTML-escaped and a
template error is a build error. Turbo and Stimulus are vendored by Forge and
loaded through the import map; no Node toolchain is needed. Every response
carries a strict Content-Security-Policy (same-origin scripts and styles, the
import map allowed by hash, no inline scripts or `style` attributes).

Every form that changes state must carry the page's CSRF token:
`forge::views::csrf_field(&token)` renders the hidden `csrf_token` input and
Turbo sends the `<meta name="csrf-token">` value in `x-csrf-token`. Unsafe
requests without a matching token are refused with `403`. A `POST` form can
tunnel `PATCH`, `PUT` or `DELETE` in a `_method` field. Decode form bodies with
`forge::web::decode_form`, answer a successful submission with
`forge::views::see_other` (`303`) and attach a message with
`forge::views::Flash`. The CSRF and flash cookies use the `__Host-` prefix
and are `Secure`: browsers accept them on `https://` and on
`http://localhost`/`127.0.0.1`.

### Translations

The pages' text is in `config/locales/*.json`, Rails I18n's layout in JSON
([guide](https://github.com/rocketinsidecorp/forge-rust/blob/main/docs/i18n.md)).
Templates use `{{ layout.i18n.t("welcome.title").with("app", application) }}`,
handlers `site.i18n(&request).t("sessions.signed_in").text()`. Each request
gets the locale of its `locale` cookie, else `Accept-Language`, else the
default (`DEFAULT_LOCALE` in `src/adapters/http/views/locales.rs`, overridden
by `FORGE_I18N_DEFAULT_LOCALE`):

```sh
curl -s -H 'Accept-Language: es' http://127.0.0.1:3000/ | grep '<h1>'
FORGE_I18N_DEFAULT_LOCALE=en cargo run
cp config/locales/en.json config/locales/fr.json   # then rename the "en" key to "fr" and translate
forge i18n check                                   # what each locale lacks; exit 1 when incomplete
```

Development and test show a missing key as `translation missing: LOCALE.KEY`
(the generated tests reject it); production falls back to the default
locale.
%%end%%

## Development

%%if database%%
This application uses %%DATABASE_LABEL%%. SQLx stays in the outer
infrastructure/bootstrap boundary; domain and application code do not depend on it.
`src/bootstrap` declares the backend once; Forge owns the connection pool, runs the
embedded migrations and reports database readiness on `/health/ready`.
%%if postgresql%%
The built-in Forge migrations create append-only audit storage first, then
principal/session/membership tables. Session bearer and CSRF values are persisted
only as 256-bit digests.
%%end%%
%%if mysql_family%%
`migrations/` starts empty. The PostgreSQL-only audit, identity, session and
tenant-membership modules were not generated for %%DATABASE_LABEL%% yet
([ADR 0021](https://github.com/rocketinsidecorp/forge-rust/blob/main/docs/adr/0021-selectable-database-backends.md)).
Tenant isolation on %%DATABASE_LABEL%% rests on the application layer: always bind the
tenant predicate from `TenantContext`. Write ids with `Id::<T>::new()` (UUIDv7) and
store them as `BINARY(16)`; the database must never generate ids.
%%end%%
%%if sqlite%%
`migrations/` starts empty. The PostgreSQL-only audit, identity, session and
tenant-membership modules were not generated for SQLite yet
([ADR 0021](https://github.com/rocketinsidecorp/forge-rust/blob/main/docs/adr/0021-selectable-database-backends.md)).
Tenant isolation on SQLite rests on the application layer: always bind the tenant
predicate from `TenantContext`. Write ids with `Id::<T>::new()` (UUIDv7) and store
them as `BLOB`; the database must never generate ids. The local database file is
`storage/development.sqlite3` (git-ignored; the directory is kept by `storage/.gitkeep`).
%%end%%

